  "body": "Eighth production-readiness stage, stacked on PR #55.\n\nScope is deliberately limited to **runtime validation where explicitly authorized**.\n\nAdds:\n- `scan-runtime-validation-plan/0.1`;\n- `scan-authorized-runtime-validation/0.1`;\n- `scan-body runtime-validate TARGET PLAN --out DIR --authorize-plan-sha256 SHA`;\n- exact plan-hash authorization before any execution;\n- temporary-copy execution;\n- shell disabled;\n- sanitized environment;\n- Linux network namespace with loopback only;\n- timeout and bounded recorded output;\n- safe relative-path assertions;\n- source-tree hash verification before/after execution;\n- runtime assertions for exit code, stdout/stderr, files, JSON probe values, hashes, and duration.\n\nAuthority boundary:\n- ordinary SCAN remains static/read-only/non-executing;\n- runtime results are sidecar observations only;\n- no scan_index.sqlite writes;\n- no automatic semantic overlay;\n- no static coverage upgrade;\n- no automatic reconstruction-anchor promotion;\n- a runtime PASS means only the exact authorized assertions passed in that run.\n\nThe CI gate proves state transition, persistence, a dynamically emitted probe value, elapsed time, secret-env non-forwarding, source immutability, wrong-hash refusal, and negative-observation preservation.\n\nOperational hardening remains the next independent roadmap stage.",
